OPENAI_API_KEY="your api key"
OPEN_AI_RESPONSES_MODEL="gpt-5-mini"
OPEN_AI_VOICE_MODEL="gpt-4o-mini-tts"
OPEN_AI_VOICE="alloy"
GENERATED_OUTPUT_DIR="./.output"
OSS_ENABLED=0
OSS_MODEL_ID=openai/gpt-oss-20b
OPENAI_CONVERT_PROMPT="
Extract an audiobook-ready transcript from a PDF and return segmented JSON for text-to-speech.

Goals:
- Clean, flowing prose in the correct reading order.
- Segments splitting at natural boundaries.
- return the entirety of the text, as this is used for study material and might be on the test.
- you may summarize text in a segment if it is excessively long, but do not omit any text.

Cleaning rules
- Remove headers, footers, page numbers, footnote markers, and line-wrap hyphenation.
- Merge lines into paragraphs. Keep chapter and section titles.
- Omit figure/table labels, decorative glyphs, and non-narrative captions.
- Normalize punctuation and spacing for TTS. Replace odd ligatures. Fix common OCR errors.
- Remove non-narrative citations and reference lists unless they are needed to understand the text.
- If the source has no clear chapters/sections, return one chapter with null titles.
- Do not include any explanation outside the JSON.
Output format:
{
  \"chapters\": [
    {
      \"title\": \"Chapter Title or null\",
      \"sections\": [
        {
          \"title\": \"Section Title or null\",
          \"segments\": [
            {
              \"text\": \"Text segment content.\"
              \"approx_words\": number of words in this segment
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
"

OPENAI_CONDENSE_PROMPT="
Extract an audiobook-ready condensed summary from a PDF and return segmented JSON for text-to-speech.

Goals:
- Clean, flowing prose in the correct reading order, condensed but containing all relevant facts.
- Segments splitting at natural boundaries.
- return everything of importance, as this is used for study material and might be on the test.

Cleaning rules
- Remove headers, footers, page numbers, footnote markers, and line-wrap hyphenation.
- Merge lines into paragraphs. Keep chapter and section titles.
- Omit figure/table labels, decorative glyphs, and non-narrative captions.
- Normalize punctuation and spacing for TTS. Replace odd ligatures. Fix common OCR errors.
- Remove non-narrative citations and reference lists unless they are needed to understand the text.
- If the source has no clear chapters/sections, return one chapter with null titles.
- Do not include any explanation outside the JSON.
Output format:
{
  \"chapters\": [
    {
      \"title\": \"Chapter Title or null\",
      \"sections\": [
        {
          \"title\": \"Section Title or null\",
          \"segments\": [
            {
              \"text\": \"Text segment content.\"
              \"approx_words\": number of words in this segment
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
"
